## Summary

Made the content-authoring skills Mermaid-aware so newly generated courses use diagrams where they genuinely improve understanding (US-216 shipped the renderer; this story tells the generators it exists).

**docs/widgets.md** — new `### Mermaid diagrams` subsection under Theory:
- Fenced ```` ```mermaid ```` syntax + supported types (flowchart, sequenceDiagram, mindmap)
- **When to use:** pipelines, data/control flow, concept maps, architectures/state machines
- **When NOT to:** formulas → KaTeX, quantitative charts → `plotImage`/`histogram`, photographic figures → inline image
- Guidelines: ~15-node limit, valid syntax, no inline `style`/`classDef` colour overrides (they fight the theme)

**Skill prompts** — added a Mermaid clause + a short flowchart example to all four skills that emit/edit theory content: `generate_lesson` (fenced ```mermaid example), `regenerate_section`, `insert_section`, `regenerate_lesson` (inline `flowchart LR; …` example). Each repeats the same guideline (valid syntax, no inline-style overrides, ≤ ~15 nodes).

**Acceptance criteria:**
- ✅ docs/widgets.md Mermaid subsection with syntax/types/when-use/when-not/size limit
- ✅ generate_lesson, regenerate_section, insert_section (+ regenerate_lesson) mention Mermaid with a flowchart example
- ✅ Prompt guidelines: correct syntax, no inline styles, ~15 nodes max
- ✅ generate_quiz_lesson intentionally unchanged — noted in the US-217 `notes` field (quiz-only lessons have no theory)
- ✅ `grep -rli mermaid` over the skills dir returns exactly the four theory-authoring skills, each with a flowchart example
- ✅ Typecheck passes (`tsc --noEmit`, clean)

`passes: true` set for US-217 and committed (`6aa217c`).
